S | Hanks’ Balanced Salts Solution HEPES Other salt solutions & Salts PBS | Phosphate Buffered Saline Company Commitments Certifications Media Formula Finder Support Articles FAQ Catalogue Contact Search EN 0 Select your Country & Language Choose your country site and preferred display language. Select your country Select your language Save changes International expertise serving the life sciences Reliable biological solutions for cell culture, worldwide. From sourcing and manufacturing through to distribution and documentation, Biowest controls every stage of its process to ensure complete traceability. Shop all products Find the right formula Origin-traced USDA Approved Certified ISO 9001:2015 Certified ISO 13485:2016 200+ Products 35+ Years in Life Sciences Global Distribution Quality Assured Origin-traced USDA Approved Certified ISO 9001:2015 Certified ISO 13485:2016 200+ Products 35+ Years in Life Sciences Global Distribution Quality Assured Our Solutions Solutions for Every Stage of Cell Culture Discover our range of serum, plasma, cell culture media, salt solutions and buffers, designed to support reliable laboratory and cell culture workflows. Sera & Plasma Discover our range of FBS and animal sera. Each manufactured batch is rigorously controlled: starting with the collection of the serum, its treatment and production, to the final packaging on our premises. Biowest analyses, classifies and tests its products before shipment to customers all over the world. Each batch is delivered with a Certificate of Analysis. The Biowest Quality System can trace raw materials back to the original supplier, place where they were collected. Biowest’s vertical integration system provides origin certification and full sera traceability. All geographical origins can be treated. Please contact us for inquiries. Animal plasma Fetal Bovine Serum (FBS) Other animal sera Serum alternative Treated sera Treated European Sera Treated South American sera View all Sera & Plasma Cell Culture Media Cell culture is the set of techniques for maintaining and growing cells outside their original tissue environment, under controlled survival conditions. It is widely used in research to study the behaviour of cells and their response to different stimuli, as well as to produce recombinant proteins and drugs. All our products are subjected to rigorous quality control tests (pH, osmolality, composition, homogeneity, glucose and sodium analysis, endotoxin, biological performance). BME | Basal Medium Eagle's CMRL 1066 DMEM | Dulbecco's Modified Eagle Medium DMEM F12 DMEM High Glucose DMEM Low Glucose GMEM | Glasgow MEM BHK 21 Ham | Nutrient medium (F10, F12) IMDM | Iscove's Modified Dulbecco's Medium Leibovitz L-15 Medium View all Cell Culture Media Cell Culture Reagents & Others Cell culture reagents are essential components for the growth and maintenance of cells in vitro, such as culture media, serum and growth factors. Other types of reagents, such as cell dissociation enzymes, will also be involved in maintaining cell quality. Their quality therefore has a significant impact on the quality of cells in culture, underlining the importance of their conservation and proper use. Accutase® Bioguard Cell Culture Water Colcemid Glucose Glutamine Lymphosep MEM Concentrate Amino Acids, Vitamins, NEAA Mycokit Trypsin View all Cell Culture Reagents & Others Salt Solutions Salt solutions maintain the osmolarity of reagents used in the laboratory and have a buffering effect on pH. They are widely used in the laboratory as washing solutions for cells prior to their dissociation or as reaction buffers for biochemical tests (ELISA) and other diagnostic techniques. In microbiology, saline solutions are also used for the preparation of culture media and for the dilution of samples in microbiology tests. Salt solutions are used: for the preparation of organ parts, during the dissociation process, to isolate cell suspensions or to prepare viral transport medium. Find all the salt solutions offered by Biowest to preserve the environment of your cells. DPBS | Dulbecco's Phosphate Buffered Saline EBSS | Earle's Balanced Salts Solution HBSS | Hanks' Balanced Salts Solution HEPES Other salt solutions & Salts PBS | Phosphate Buffered Saline View all Salt Solutions Bovine Serum Albumin Bovine Serum Albumin (BSA) is a little protein of 66kDa present in animal serum and makes up approximately 60% of all proteins. Because of its negative charge, Bovine Serum Albumin binds water, salts, fatty acids, vitamins and hormones and carries these bound components between tissues and cells. Albumins are frequently used as stabilizers for other solubilized proteins (e.g., labile enzymes). Due to its high stability and less interference with biological activities, BSA is used on many biochemical applications such as Immunochemistry and Western-Blot or ELISA, in which it is used as a blocking reagent. BSA Fraction V - 30% Liquid BSA Fraction V - Fatty Acids Free BSA Fraction V - Lyophilised pH ~7 BSA Fraction V - Protease Free Lyophilised View all Bovine Serum Albumin Antibiotics Use antibiotics to preserve and protect your cells by getting rid of micro-organisms. Antibiotics should not be used routinely but only for short-term applications as their continued use encourages the development of antibiotic-resistant strains. In addition, some antibiotics can cross-react with cells and interfere with the cellular processes being studied. Amphotericin B Antibiotic-Antimycotic G-418 Gentamicin Sulfate Glutamine-Penicillin-Streptomycin Nanomycopulitine® Penicillin-Streptomycin View all Antibiotics Human products Discover Biowest’s range of human-origin products, including HIV-tested human serum, HIV-tested male AB human serum, pooled human plasma, and human serum albumin. Human serum and plasma are collected from voluntary donors and processed in accordance with European regulations. Each batch is double 0.2 µm filtered and tested for HBs, HCV, and HIV-1/2. The country of collection is listed on the certificate of analysis. Important: Human-origin products must be considered as potentially infectious and handled accordingly. View all Human products Our Process Our processes are designed for continuity - sourcing to delivery Certified ISO 9001:2015, and ISO 13485:2016, traceability is a major component of these audits. Each batch of sterile filtered serum is controlled internally, from the importation of the raw serum, to final filtration and labelling. Copies of all documentation are available in hard copy and electronic format. Our Commitments 01 Animal Collection Blood collected under EU Regulation. BSE status verified before processing. Geographic origin confirmed. 02 Processing & QC Testing Filtration, treatment, and quality testing run under ISO-certified conditions. No batch is released until it passes the panel it was assigned. 03 Documentation & Dispatch CoA, health certificate, EDQM certificate, and certificate of origin issued per lot The Latest Advancing Cell Culture through Knowledge Connect with us at events around the world or stay up to date with expert insights and the latest in cell culture. Mechanisms of Exosome-Supplemented WJ-MSC Therapy in Degenerative Disc Disease: Integrating Proteomic Profiling with Clinical Functional Recovery Authors Alejandro Toro-Rivera, Wendy V. Jaraba-Álvarez, Angélica M. Calle-Ramírez, Juan P. Franco-Salazar, Luz Adriana Palacio, Daniela Martínez-Penaloza, Julián España, Karolynn Halpert, Hector Ortega-Arellano and Víctor Gómez Abstracts Background: Degenerative disc disease (DDD) is a primary cause of chronic back pain and disability globally. Although Wharton’s jelly-derived mesenchymal stromal cells (WJ-MSCs) possess proven therapeutic potential, the added clinical value of supplementing… FBS Articles Quotes / Publications October 2, 2026 Biowest at IABS 2026 Biowest at IABS 2026 On September 29 and 30, 2026, join Biowest online for the international scientific meeting organized by IABS Europe, dedicated to bovine serum. Biowest is proud to sponsor this 100% virtual meeting focused on“Bovine Serum: Challenges and opportunities in the research and development and manufacture of vaccines and other biological products.” What you can expect The scientific… Biowest News September 23, 2026 Reduced DDB2 Expression Is Associated with Temozolomide Resistance in Glioblastoma Cells Authors Inés Grávalos-Cano, Teresa Morales-Ruiz, Rafael R. Ariza, Teresa Roldán-Arjona and María Isabel Martínez-Macías Abstracts Glioblastoma (GBM) remains one of the most lethal primary brain tumours, and resistance to temozolomide (TMZ), the standard chemotherapeutic agent for GBM, represents a major obstacle to effective treatment. Although O6-methylguanine-DNA methyltransferase (MGMT) is a well-established determinant of TMZ response, MGMT status alone does not… Quotes / Publications July 8, 2026 We will be present at Euromit from May 31 to June 4, 2026 Biowest at Euromit 2026 From May 31 to June 4, 2026, meet Biowest in Angers for Euromit, the international conference dedicated to mitochondria and mitochondrial diseases. Biowest will be there to support you in your research and cell culture projects. What you can expect at our stand: Stand 11 Our experts will be available to: Present our wide range of… Biowest News May 25, 2026 Biowest will be present at Analytica, Munich from March 24 to 27, 2026 BIOWEST NEWS 10/03/2026 Come and meet us at Analytica 2026 We are excited to announce that Biowest will be exhibiting at Analytica 2026, the world’s leading trade fair for laboratory technology, analysis, and biotechnology. Join our team of experts to discuss your cell culture needs and discover our latest range of high-quality sera and media. Booth : 112 (Hall A3)… Biowest News March 10, 2026 Serving Life Sciences since 1987 Our products are used in the production of biopharmaceuticals and vaccines, as well as in the academic, government, and industrial research sectors. They cover areas such as cell biology, genomics, proteomics, virology, immunology, innovative drug research, and toxicology. Over 200 trusted products A global distribution network A full integrated supply chain Explore our Products Your Cell Culture partner for over 35 years. Rue de la Caille 49340 Nuaillé, France biowest@biowest.net (+33) 241 464 242 Product Categories Antibiotics Bovine Serum Albumin Cell Culture Media Cell Culture Reagents & Others Human products Salt Solutions Sera & Plasma About Us About Us Distributors Commitments / CSR Certifications Media Recruitment Support Articles FAQ Catalogue Marketing materials Logistics & Reception Find Formula Formula finder Legal Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Privacy settings Other HTML Sitemap Copyright © 2026 Biowest | All rights reserved Clear Suggestions Product Results Documents See all search results Select your Country & Language Choose your country site and preferred display language. Select your country Select your language Save changes WordPress Cookie Plugin by Real Cookie Banner 
