+ Medium data Medium data Search for medium no. = [266]. Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min. 266 METHANOMICROBIUM MOBILE MEDIUM Rumen fluid, clarified (see below) 300.0 ml KH 2 PO 4 0.3 g K 2 HPO 4 0.3 g (NH 4 ) 2 SO 4 0.3 g NaCl 0.6 g MgSO 4 ·7H 2 O 0.13 g CaCl 2 ·2H 2 O 8.0 mg Trace minerals (see Medium No. 151 ) 10.0 ml Trace vitamins (see Medium No. 197 ) 10.0 ml FeSO 4 ·7H 2 O 2.0 mg NaHCO 3 2.0 g Yeast extract (BD-Difco) 1.0 g Trypticase peptone (BD-BBL) 1.0 g Fatty acid mixture (see below) 20.0 ml Resazurin 1.0 mg Na 2 S·9H 2 O 0.5 g L-Cysteine·HCl·H 2 O 0.5 g Distilled water 660.0 ml Mix ingredients, except NaHCO 3 , L-cysteine·HCl·H 2 O and Na 2 S·9H 2 O, and adjust pH to 6.5. Bring to a boil for 5-10 sec, then, cool down under a stream of H 2 -CO 2 (80:20, v/v) and add NaHCO 3 to the medium. Dispense the medium into suitable culture vessels (e.g., 20 ml of the medium in 120 ml serum bottles) under a stream of H 2 -CO 2 (80:20, v/v) and seal with butyl rubber stoppers. After autoclaving, stand the medium overnight. Separately autoclave cysteine·HCl and Na 2 S·9H 2 O as 5% solutions, respectively, under a N 2 atmosphere. Prior to inoculation, aseptically and anaerobically add the L-cysteine·HCl·H 2 O and Na 2 S·9H 2 O solutions. Pressurize the inoculated bottles to 200 kPa H 2 -CO 2 (80:20, v/v). To prepare the clarified rumen fluid, preheat rumen content at 120C for 15 min. Use the supernatant after centrifuging at 25,000 x g for 15 min. Fatty acid mixture: Valeric acid 0.5 g Isovaleric acid 0.5 g α-Methylbutyric acid 0.5 g Isobutyric acid 0.5 g Distilled water 20.0 ml Adjust pH to 7.5 with concentrated NaOH solution. Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved 
