+ Medium data Medium data Search for medium no. = [1476]. Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min. 1476 MODIFIED UREAPLASMA MEDIUM PPLO broth w/o Crystal Violet (BD-Difco 255420) 2.1 g 1% Phenol red solution (see below) 200.0 µl Distilled water 85.0 ml Mix components, adjust pH to 6.0-6.2. After autoclaving and then cooling to 50-55C, aseptically add the following solutions (filter-sterilized). Bovine calf serum (heat-inactivated) 5.0 ml 4M Urea - 4% yeast extract solution (see below) 10.0 ml 1% Phenol red solution: Dissolve 1.0 g phenol red first in 10-20 ml of 0.1 N NaOH. Then adjust volume to 100 ml. After filter-sterilizing, store at 4C. 4M Urea - 4% yeast extract solution: Urea 24.0 g Yeast extract 4.0 g Distilled water 100.0 ml Mix components, sterilize by filtration through a 0.22 µm filter and store at 4C. Dispense the medium into sterilized plastic tubes (e.g., 5 ml medium in 15 ml of plastic tubes) and add 100-200 µl of culture solution. Incubate the cultures at 37C for 1-3 days. When the color of the medium turns from yellow to orange or red, subculture into the new medium. After color change, the strain can be stored at 4C for 1-2 weeks. Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved 
