+ Medium data Medium data Search for medium no. = [187]. Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min. 187 DESULFUROCOCCUS AMYLOLYTICUS MEDIUM NH 4 Cl 0.33 g KH 2 PO 4 0.33 g KCl 0.33 g CaCl 2 ·2H 2 O 0.44 g MgCl 2 ·6H 2 O 0.7 g NaCl 0.5 g NaHCO 3 0.8 g FeCl 2 solution (see below) 1.0 ml Trace element solution (see below) 1.0 ml Trace vitamins (see Medium No. 197 ) 10.0 ml Yeast extract (BD-Difco) 0.2 g Bacto peptone (BD-Difco) 5.0 g Sulfur (powder) 10.0 g Na 2 S·9H 2 O 0.5 g Resazurin 1.0 mg Distilled water 990.0 ml Mix ingredients, except yeast extract, peptone, vitamins, sulfur and Na 2 S·9H 2 O, and autoclave under a N 2 -CO 2 (80:20) atmosphere. Separately autoclave yeast extract and peptone as 10% solutions and Na 2 S·9H 2 O as a 5% solution under a N 2 atmosphere. Steam sulfur for 3 hr on each of 3 successive days. Filter-sterilize NaHCO 3 as an 8% solution and vitamin solution while gassing with N 2 . Aseptically and anaerobically add yeast extract, peptone, NaHCO 3 and vitamin solutions, and sulfur to the medium under a N 2 -CO 2 (80:20) atmosphere. Prior to inoculation, add the sterile Na 2 S·9H 2 O solution, and adjust pH to 6.2-6.4 with sterile 1 N H 2 SO 4 . FeCl 2 solution: 25% HCl (7.7 M) 10.0 ml FeCl 2 ·4H 2 O 1.5 g Distilled water 990.0 ml Trace element solution: ZnCl 2 70.0 mg MnCl 2 ·4H 2 O 100.0 mg H 3 BO 3 6.0 mg CoCl 2 ·6H 2 O 190.0 mg CuCl 2 ·2H 2 O 2.0 mg NiCl 2 ·6H 2 O 24.0 mg Na 2 MoO 4 ·2H 2 O 36.0 mg Distilled water 1.0 L Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved 
