+ P5: RS Medium - Nutrient Medium (NM) Component | Media | MediaDive × Settings Language English Deutsch Motion-sickness mode This mode reduces motion and animations on the page. Dyslexia mode The web page uses a special font to increase readibility for user with dyslexia. We use browser cookies to save your preferences. Apply --> × Ingredient name × Home Media P5: RS Medium - Nutrient Medium (NM) Component Accessibility Options Accessibility Language English Deutsch High contrast Enhance the contrast of the web page for better readability. Reduce motion Reduce motion and animations on the page. Dyslexia mode Use a special font to increase readability for users with dyslexia. Apply Manual Contact Content Media Solutions Ingredients Strains Steps Gas Search Medium finder Solution finder Taxonomy search Isolation sources Tools Medium builder SPARQL endpoint Unit converter Compare media Compare solutions Prediction SOON × Leave a comment Your name (optional) Your mail address (optional) Your mail address will not be made public, but allows out team to contact you regarding your comment. Publish comment Comments for this medium No comments for this medium. Close --> Download --> Download Adjust volume (optional) Multiply × Main sol. ml Create PDF Other formats Text JSON Comments (count($comments)) --> Feedback Guided tour --> Guided tour PUBLIC P5 P5 . RS Medium - Nutrient Medium (NM) Component User-provided medium : This medium was provided by one of our users. Please be aware that we do not curate or test the media that are composed by our users. Be cautious when trying this medium, especially since no valid reference is given. Validation is running ... Validation is complete. You may need to refresh the page or go to the viewing page to see the results. Culture medium recipe Vol. × RS Medium - Nutrient Medium (NM) Component # ml Equipment needed: Autoclave Autoclavable bottles 0.22 µm vaccum filters 0.22 µm syringe filters 50 ml conical tubes Compound Amount Unit Conc. [g/L] Conc. [mM] Na 2 SiO 3 x 5 H 2 O (Single stock in H 2 O. Autoclave and store at RT.) 0.4500 g/50ml - - FeCl 3 x 6 H 2 O (Single stock in H 2 O. Autoclave and store at RT.) 0.0600 g/50ml - - Na2EDTA x 2H2O (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at RT.) 0.0900 g/50ml - - NaNO 3 (Single stock in NNM. Filter and store at RT.) 1.5000 g/50ml - - NaH 2 PO 4 x H 2 O (Single stock in NNM. Filter and store at RT.) 1.0000 g/50ml - - K 2 HPO 4 (Single stock in H 2 O. Filter and store at RT.) 2.0000 g/50ml - - NH 4 Cl (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at RT.) 0.0500 g/50ml - - Thiamine HCl (B 1 ) (Single stock in H 2 O. Filter and store at -20C.) 0.0500 g/ml - - Biotin (B 8 ) (Single stock in H 2 O. Filter and store at -20C.) 0.0001 g/ml - - Cyanocobalamin (B 12 ) (Single stock in H 2 O. Filter and store at -20C.) 0.0010 g/ml - - Folic acid (B 9 ) (Single stock in H 2 O. Filter and store at -20C.) 0.0010 g/ml - - Pyridoxine (B 6 ) (Single stock in H 2 O. Filter and store at -20C.) 0.0010 g/ml - - Riboflavin (B 2 ) (Single stock in H 2 O. Filter and store at -20C.) 0.0010 g/ml - - Niacin (B 3 ) (Single stock in H 2 O. Filter and store at -20C.) 0.0010 g/ml - - D-pantothenate acid hemicalcium salt (B 5 ) (Single stock in H 2 O. Filter and store at -20C.) 0.0010 g/ml - - Myo-Inositol (B 7 ) (Single stock in H 2 O. Filter and store at -20C.) 0.0010 g/ml - - 4-Aminobenzoic Acid (Single stock in H 2 O. Filter and store at -20C.) 0.0010 g/ml - - L-Glutamine (Single stock in H 2 O. Autoclave and store at -20C.) 0.6000 g/50ml - - Glycerol (Add directly to Mix solution 5 (Carbon Sources)) 45.0000 µl - - Sodium pyruvate (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at 4C in the dark.) 1.9800 g/50ml - - D-Glucose (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at 4C.) 1.9800 g/50ml - - N-acetyl-D-glucosamine (Single stock in H 2 O. Autoclave and store at -20C.) 1.5900 g/50ml - - D-Ribose (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at 4C.) 2.0000 g/50ml - - Sodium succinate (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at RT.) 2.7200 g/50ml - - y-aminobutyric acid (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at -20C.) 1.5500 g/50ml - - Sodium acetate (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at RT.) 1.2300 g/50ml - - Decanoic acid (Single stock in H 2 O. Autoclave and store at RT.) 0.0070 g/50ml - - L-Arabinose (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at 4C.) 1.3200 g/50ml - - L-Rhamnose (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at 4C.) 1.8100 g/50ml - - Fucose (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at 4C.) 3.6100 g/50ml - - D-Mannose (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at 4C.) 3.9600 g/50ml - - Galactose (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at 4C.) 1.9800 g/50ml - - D-Xylose (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at 4C.) 8.0000 g/50ml - - Sodium alginate (Single stock in H 2 O. Autoclave and store at 4C.) 0.0900 g/50ml - - Methyl-cellulose (See notes below) 1.0200 g/50ml - - Pectin (See notes below) 2.0000 g/50ml - - Guanosine (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at -20C.) 0.0300 g/50ml - - Uracil (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at -20C.) 0.1600 g/50ml - - MEM 50X Amino Acids solution (Sigma) (Add directly to Mix solution 4 (Amino Acids)) 2.2500 ml - - MEM 100X Amino Acids solution (Sigma) (Add directly to Mix solution 4 (Amino Acids)) 2.2700 ml - - 1 2 Single stock phase: Prepare the single stocks as reported above. Single stocks are prepared either in purified H 2 O or in the Non-Nutrient Medium (NNM) component of RS Medium (see accompanying protocol on MediaDive). Filtration is performed with a 0.22 µm pore size. 3 Single stock phase: Notes for Methyl cellulose: prepare the single stock in H 2 O. It is known that Methyl cellulose is soluble in cold water and insoluble in hot water. In order to prepare this stock, add the relative amount and shake the single stock from time to time for 20 minutes. Leave the stock in cold water overnight. Its color should be white. The day after, after autoclaving, it will result like a white solid, not liquid. Leave it at RT until it becomes liquid and transparent. Store at 4C. 4 Single stock phase: Notes for Pectin: prepare the single stock in H 2 O. To dissolve, use a hot plate heater with a magnetic stirrer for 20 minutes before autoclaving. Store at 4C. 5 Mix solutions phase: Mix solution 1 (Si and Fe+EDTA): add 2.27 ml each from the single stocks of Na 2 SiO 3 *5H2O, FeCl 3 *6H2O and Na2EDTA*2H2O. Fill to 50 ml with NNM. Filter via syringe through a 0.22 µm pore size. Store at 4C. 6 Mix solutions phase: Mix solution 2 (NO 3 -PO 4 ): add 2.27 ml each from the single stocks of NaNO 3 , NaH2PO 4 *H 2 O, K2HPO 4 and NH 4 Cl. Fill to 50 ml with NNM. Filter via syringe through a 0.22 µm pore size. Prepare this mix fresh every time. 7 Mix solutions phase: Mix solution 3 (Vitamins): add 4.5 µl each from the single stocks of vitamins (Thiamine HCl (B 1 ), Biotin (B 8 ), Cyanocobalamin (B 1 2), Folic acid (Folate) (B 9 ), Pyridoxine (B 6 ), Riboflavin (B 2 ), Niacin (B 3 ), D-pantothenate acid hemicalcium salt (B 5 ), Myo-Inositol (B 7 ) and 4-Aminobenzoic acid). Fill to 50 ml with NNM. Filter via syringe through a 0.22 µm pore size. Store at 4C. 8 Mix solutions phase: Mix solution 4 (Amino Acids): add 2.25 ml from the MEM 50X Amino Acids solution from Sigma and 2.27 ml from the MEM 100X Amino Acids solution from Sigma. Add 2.27 ml of the single stock of Glutamine. Fill to 50 ml with NNM. Filter via syringe through a 0.22 µm pore size. Store at 4C. NOTES: The MEM 50X AA solution contains Arginine (6.32 g/L), Cysteine HCl (1.56 g/L), Histidine (2.10 g/L), L-Isoleucine (2.63 g/L), L-Leucine (2.62 g/L), Lysine HCl (3.63 g/L), L-Methionine (0.76 g/L), L-Phenylalanine (1.65 g/L), L-Threonine (2.38 g/L), L-Tryptophan (0.51 g/L), L-Tyrosine (1.80 g/L) and L-Valine (2.34 g/L). The MEM 100X AA solution contains L-Alanine (0.89 g/L), Glycine (0.75 g/L), L-Proline (1.15 g/L), L-Asparagine*H 2 O (1.50 g/L), Aspartate (1.33 g/L), Glutamate (1.47 g/L), Serine (1.05 g/L). 9 Mix solutions phase: Mix solution 5 (Carbon Sources): add 45 µl of Glycerol from Sigma (1.26 g/mL). Add 2.27 ml of each carbon source (Sodium pyruvate, D-glucose, N-acetyI-D-glucosamine, D-ribose, Sodium succinate, y-aminobutyric acid, Sodium acetate, Decanoic acid, L-arabinose, L-rhamnose, Fucose, L-mannose, Galactose, Xylan, Sodium alginate, Methyl-cellulose, Pectin, Guanosine and Uracil). Fill to 50 ml with NNM. Filter through a 0.22 µm pore size by using the vacuum filter (not by syringe) because the solution is viscous. Store at 4C. 10 Final phase: Combine 4 ml of Mix solution 1 (Si and Fe+EDTA), 30 ml from Mix solution 2 (NO 3 -PO 4 ), 10.7 ml from Mix solution 3 (Vitamins), 10.9 ml of Mix solution 4 (Amino Acids) and 10.7 ml of Mix solution 5 (Carbon sources). Fill to 150 ml with NNM. Filter through a 0.22 µm pore size by using a vacuum filter. Store Nutrient Medium 1.0 (NM 1.0) component at 4C. 11 Acknowledgements: We would like to thank Ben Temperton (University of Exteter) for fundamental advice and ideas in the creation of RS medium. Metadata Creator: Cristiana Sigona Author(s): Cristiana Sigona, Daniel J. Richter Published: 30.06.23 Last modified: 07.10.25 Source: Media Dive : public Medium type: Complex medium Final pH: 7 Equipment needed: Autoclave, Autoclavable bottles, 0.22 µm vaccum filters, 0.22 µm syringe filters, 50 ml conical tubes Description: The RS medium is a fully defined medium designed for growing diverse marine protists. RS medium presents a natural buffer system with a pH of ~7 and a salinity of 3,3%. It includes two components: the Non-Nutrient Medium (NNM) and the Nutrient Medium 1.0 (NM 1.0). Here we show the preparation of the NM 1.0 Show QR code for mobile --> Edit in Medium builder Associated strains Have some cookies! We are using cookies to improve the user experience. We save the following information: user preferences for language, accessibility, help features and medium favourites. Unfortunately, you cannot use this site if you don't agree. I agree Not found what you were looking for? Search within all databases of the DSMZ Digital Diversity provided to you by Media Dive About News Cite Statistics MediaRegistry --> Help Website Medium builder API reference Contact Social Media Linkedin YouTube If Media Dive was useful to you, please participate in this 2-minute survey: Survey © DSMZ 2026 Imprint Privacy Statement License Sitemap --> 
